{"id": "EUVD-2026-59520", "enisaUuid": "39505eef-e048-3481-88cc-5f9f98c46edd", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmd/raid1,raid10: fix bio accounting for split md cloned bios\n\nUse md_cloned_bio() to control bio accounting instead of relying\non r1bio_existed in raid1 or the io_accounting flag in raid10.\n\nThe previous logic does not reliably reflect whether a bio is an\nmd cloned bio. When a failed bio is split and resubmitted via\nbio_submit_split_bioset() on the error path, this can lead to either\ndouble accounting for md cloned bios, or missing accounting for bios\nreturned from bio_submit_split_bioset()\n\nFix this by using md_cloned_bio() to detect md cloned bios and\nskip accounting accordingly.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:58:52", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:45:30", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/91d0fc000d8cc40fcb4285e6160dd1ce98c56201", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/235d16ae715104b981a4fbc9434398e3816773b1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bcf30e14d2bd509c57e93021b46aedc878896e7b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bb8d7ea74206b419aa05d7773a15a923b668c9f0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ba976e3501111d11c550848b3b7341a73035f582"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-74373", "GHSA-w5h2-43j2-4p8f"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "29cf38ea-583c-32f6-a16c-733b094969c4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bb2a9acefaf9ce5bbc1e70f407e34599233d0243 <ba976e3501111d11c550848b3b7341a73035f582"}, {"id": "3f7e8548-438f-3378-8b9b-a283ae705a60", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "43bd9560-4e10-3eaa-a86e-946708c4730f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "4d9db924-3700-3a37-a0d6-a0e2703bab87", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "55efeaae-ff5e-3ef8-b742-f0a369bbf30e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bb2a9acefaf9ce5bbc1e70f407e34599233d0243 <bb8d7ea74206b419aa05d7773a15a923b668c9f0"}, {"id": "56dc883b-c1ef-3ed9-86a7-ca8ae929a788", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6"}, {"id": "593f46b3-8067-39ef-8c7f-73725f3e877f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bb2a9acefaf9ce5bbc1e70f407e34599233d0243 <91d0fc000d8cc40fcb4285e6160dd1ce98c56201"}, {"id": "86c2b20a-bcb8-37f9-a150-65b4a345f362", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bb2a9acefaf9ce5bbc1e70f407e34599233d0243 <235d16ae715104b981a4fbc9434398e3816773b1"}, {"id": "bbdcfa91-f0c6-35c8-b5b4-a6ba034f3633", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "d717195e-2bf2-37f2-8029-a30467d8f887", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bb2a9acefaf9ce5bbc1e70f407e34599233d0243 <bcf30e14d2bd509c57e93021b46aedc878896e7b"}, {"id": "e9ea7a55-d0ce-3a79-9a82-f740cf13ebae", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "ea4b6df2-88c4-3705-bda6-52f708cecd4c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b441c338-6788-3e91-a226-45aff9ac68e3", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}